    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338-a1">

                <pb facs="0593" n="553" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg553"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 15, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks the receipt of jour note of the 5th instant, stating that the government
                    of the United States has been apprised of the landing of a <pb facs="0594"
                        n="554" xml:id="pg554"/> cargo of four hundred African negroes, between the
                    28th and 30th of July last, at La Enseñada de Cochinas, to the westward of
                    Cienfaegos, in the island of Cuba, and that Mr. Bunch, her Majesty’s judge at
                    the Havana, intended to call the attention of the captain general to this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq.<hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
